  "question": {
    "text": "The molar conductivity at infinite dilution of&nbsp;barium chloride, sulphuric arid and hydrochloric acid are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>280</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>860</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>426</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Scm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;respectively. The molar conductivity at&nbsp;infinite dilution of barium sulphate is ___&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Scm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;( Round off to the Nearest&nbsp;Integer)."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "288",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From Kohlrausch&#39;s law</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mfenced><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mfenced><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mfenced><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mfenced><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mfenced><msub><mi>BaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8734;</mo></msubsup><mo>(</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>280</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>860</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>426</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>288</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Scm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
